  "context": "Found by trunk UAT calibration on 2026-11-06. Evidence artifacts: release-uat-trunk-525361b2f8b97f8d750b2faaab8d3f9f3a750d2e-stage3-olap and -stage3-postgres-family (cells.jsonl, per-cell logs). Heavy runs only through lock-taking entry points. DECISION GATE: any change to Doris load strictness or filter ratio goes to the owner.\n\nProgress 2026-11-06 (local UAT reproduction, Apple container/mocker on macOS arm64, develop c2bdd8bc67):\n- doris clickbench SF0.01: REPRODUCED with the harness (make uat-cell, Doris 4.0.3-all-slim started from the compose entrypoint script via `container run`; mocker compose cannot start the Doris FE here: entrypoint override ignored, FE gets -Xmx8g). Same `[DATA_QUALITY_ERROR] Encountered unqualified data` as CI. Root cause: Stream Load columns header maps every field with nullif(tmp_i,'') regardless of the dialect null marker; ClickBench writes empty strings as \"\" and NULL as __NULL__, so with trim_double_quotes every empty string became NULL and hits NOT NULL columns rejected all rows. Introduced by 9d675b4038 (#3949, perf(doris): stream TPC files as-is and null empty fields server-side). Fix: nullif against dialect.null_marker (commit on branch fix/doris-clickbench-mooncake-flightdata-load). After fix: doris clickbench, flightdata, tpch, datavault, nyctaxi SF0.01 all pass locally. No strict mode / max_filter_ratio / validation change.\n- pg-mooncake flightdata SF0.01: NOT reproduced locally. Passed standalone, in the CI cell order (all 0.01 cells before it incl. metadata_primitives, minus joinorder 1.0), and 3x re-run in the same container (DB drop/recreate path). #3949/#3950 cannot change the loaded bytes: prepare_local_load_file output for flights.csv.zst is byte-identical to the pre-#3949 per-line rewrite, and #3950 does not touch the PostgreSQL path. SQL/DDL/docker image digest unchanged between the 0.5.0 and trunk UAT runs. The CI failure is inside Moonlink (replication channel closed during mooncake.create_table of flights); the re-run signature (staging table present, flights/airlines empty, `flights already exists` on restore) points to state left by the first (quiet, unlogged) attempt, whose error is not in the evidence.\n\nCloseout 2026-11-06: Doris half merged. PR #3982 (https://github.com/BenchBox-dev/benchbox/pull/3982), merge commit 590159ea78ea7fef73e0dffdc986e102e2921325. Root cause 9d675b4038 (#3949): Stream Load columns header used nullif(tmp_i,'') for every dialect, so ClickBench's quoted empty strings became NULL and failed hits NOT NULL columns. Fix maps the dialect null marker; regression tests in tests/unit/platforms/test_doris_stream_load_null_handling.py (HTTP body+headers boundary, single and chunked) fail before / pass after. Local UAT (Apple container, Doris 4.0.3-all-slim): clickbench SF0.01 failed on develop c2bdd8bc67 with the CI data quality error, passes after; doris flightdata/tpch/datavault/nyctaxi SF0.01 also pass. Strict mode, max_filter_ratio and validation untouched.\nMooncake half NOT resolved, item left open: pg-mooncake flightdata SF0.01 does not reproduce locally on develop (standalone; full CI cell order minus joinorder 1.0 with one DB and replication slot per cell; 3x re-run in one container; 3x under mem_limit 2g/cpus 1). #3949/#3950 are not the cause: prepare_local_load_file output for flights.csv.zst is byte-identical to the pre-#3949 rewrite and #3950 does not touch the PostgreSQL path; DDL, image digest and docker config unchanged between the 0.5.0 and trunk UAT runs; flightdata is seeded (42). The CI failure is inside Moonlink (replication channel closed in mooncake.create_table of flights); the evidence only holds the diagnostic re-run (leftover __bb_moon_src_flights, flights/airlines empty), whose failure follows from state of the first quiet attempt, whose error is not captured. Next step: rerun the trunk UAT postgres-family stage with verbose logging for the first attempt (or capture the pg-mooncake container log) to learn the first error before changing code.\nSeparate unrelated finding: tests/unit/test_heavy_choke_points.py tests using the default stub machine name 'm' fail under pytest-xdist (the linux_machine cleanup sees sibling tests' `linux_machine_run.sh m` processes and leaves the machine running); reproduced locally with -n 4 and failed the ubuntu 3.14 fast leg 5 times on this PR before a rebase passed. Introduced with #3972; fix is a unique STUB_MACHINE per test as lines 333/424 already do.\n\nTrunk UAT run https://github.com/BenchBox-dev/BenchBox/actions/runs/42718296767 at develop 52615914002012e24405b77b830dc98d35ba50e9 (attempt 1): 709/710 cells passed; the only failure was pandas-df write_primitives SF1 (segfault, unrelated). pg-mooncake: 15/15 selected cells passed, including FlightData SF0.01; the earlier failure did not recur. Root cause and loader-boundary regression test are still not established, so the failure may be intermittent.\n\nRevalidated 2026-11-11 (develop c7b75c80bc): still required for the Mooncake half only; the Doris half is closed by #3982 (590159ea78, regression tests in tests/unit/platforms/test_doris_stream_load_null_handling.py) and its clickbench cell passes in trunk UAT. Acceptance line 2 (both cells pass in a hosted harness run) is now met by run 42718296767 (15/15 pg-mooncake cells incl. FlightData SF0.01, Doris 21/21) and by the scheduled trunk UAT runs 42789483182 (2026-11-10) and 42990393684 (2026-11-11), both success on attempt 1 with the postgres-family shard 'postgresql,pg-duckdb,pg-mooncake,timescaledb' (trunk-uat.yml:274) and the olap shard in the matrix; the Moonlink 'channel closed' failure from run 42266293613 has not recurred in those three runs (I have run-level conclusions only; the jobs API returned 502). Still open: line 1 (Mooncake root cause with the introducing commit) and line 3 (a regression test for the Mooncake cause). The failure was never reproduced locally and #3949/#3950 were ruled out, so unless it recurs the owner may prefer to downgrade this to a watch item; I left priority unchanged. The unrelated test_heavy_choke_points xdist stub-name flake noted on 2026-11-06 is not part of this item and its fix status was not checked.\n\n2026-11-23 closeout: BenchBox-dev/benchbox#4466 merged (9b3087d404). Delivered for the pg_mooncake half: a failed mirror attempt no longer leaves a stale staging table that turns the next attempt into `relation already exists`, the restore-failure warning carries the original mirror error, and the UAT harness keeps pg-mooncake container evidence before teardown. Acceptance line 1 (root cause with introducing commit) is NOT met for the Moonlink channel-closed failure: it was not reproduced and has not recurred. That remaining work is tracked on pg-mooncake-moonlink-channel-closed-cause-on-recurrence-20261123.",
  "description": "The first trunk UAT run (42266293613, testing develop 525361b2f8) failed two cells that passed in the v0.5.0 release UAT (run 42133357291, dfe585e094) the same day: (1) doris clickbench SF0.01: Stream Load failed with `[DATA_QUALITY_ERROR] Encountered unqualified data` and no rows loaded into `hits`; (2) pg-mooncake flightdata SF0.01: `create_table failed: Rpc(... Moonlink connector error (permanent) ... mpsc channel send error ... channel closed)` after `Could not restore the heap table name flights after a mirror failure: relation \"flights\" already exists`. Prime suspect: #3949 (native bulk load paths for local file prep, Doris, Databend and Firebolt Core), merged after 0.5.0; also check #3950 for the mooncake path. The Doris image tag is unchanged (4.0.3-all-slim). Reproduce with the UAT harness, name the root cause of each, and fix without loosening strict mode, max_filter_ratio or any validation.",
